A revoke made through a slot of the table its caller's process mounts second
looks for that slot in the first table, so a revoke that takes the second table's mount goes on,
and stops where the caller cannot make the call again.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call stopped where its caller cannot make it again

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -256,7 +256,7 @@ bool cap_revoke_below(struct cap *root, uint32_t through, bool preempt)
          * the caller could not make the call again, so an interrupt must not decide how far it got.
          * A table slot of its process can only be cleared here, never filled, so the number still names the same slot.
          */
-        const struct cap *at = slot_at(core_self()->current, through);
+        const struct cap *at = slot_at(core_self()->current, slot_index(through));
         if (at == NULL || at->type == CAP_NONE) {
             return true;
         }
